# R tidyverse style

Follow the [tidyverse style guide](https://style.tidyverse.org) for all R in
this repository.

- Prefer tidyverse idioms (`dplyr`, `tidyr`, `purrr`, `ggplot2`, `readr`, `tibble`)
  when they fit the task.
- Use the native pipe `|>` (not `%>%`).
- 2-space indentation; aim for ~80-character lines.
- Use `snake_case` for objects and functions.
- Prefer named intermediate objects over deeply nested one-liners when clearer.
- Style-only edits must preserve behavior.

Project pointers: `AGENTS.md`, `.github/instructions/r-style.instructions.md`,
`.github/copilot-instructions.md`.
